window.docContents[13].resolve({"/rules/PL1002/#PL1002-fix":{"contents":"1. Replace the sorry or admit with a complete proof.2. If the hole comes from an imported declaration, fix or replace that dependency; imported holes are not exempt.3. For an open target, write def Target : Prop := … and prove Target → Result, which states exactly what is established.\n\n","context":"Plumb for Lean rule reference\u0009Rule index\u0009PL1002: Proof holes are forbidden","header":"How to fix it","id":"/rules/PL1002/#PL1002-fix"},"/rules/PL2001/#PL2001-fix":{"contents":"1. Read the original setup error in the diagnostic detail and fix it: a missing path dependency, an unresolvable Git revision, or a toolchain that does not match lean-toolchain.2. Provision pinned dependencies (for example lake exe cache get for Mathlib) before auditing; provisioning is setup, not verification.3. Rerun the audit; a new run produces new, complete evidence.\n\n","context":"Plumb for Lean rule reference\u0009Rule index\u0009PL2001: The declared Lean environment must be available","header":"How to fix it","id":"/rules/PL2001/#PL2001-fix"}});